# HTML always revalidates (no-cache): every page, with or without .html (the
# /ad/ and /c/ad/ aerodrome pages are linked as .html), so a new deploy is seen on the next load.
# Versioned and static assets cache for a year (immutable). Their ?v= is the
# content hash written by tools/version_assets.js; npm test fails if one is stale.
# Page rules never overlap asset rules, so Netlify never merges two Cache-Control values.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, max-age=0, must-revalidate
